 654: /**
 655:  * Reflectance at normal incidence. Water is 0.02; this is deliberately
 656:  * higher. The camera sits at ~45°, where physical Fresnel gives ~0.03 and
 657:  * the sky in the water is invisible - and a puddle that reflects nothing is
 658:  * exactly the "black paint" this exists to fix. Water in games is drawn
 659:  * more reflective than it is for the same reason it is drawn bluer.
 660:  */
 661: const REFLECT_F0 = 0.12;
 662: 
 663: /** Sun glint and torch glint gains on top of the Fresnel share. */
 664: const SUN_GLINT = 1.4;
 665: const TORCH_GLINT = 2.2;
 666: 
 667: /**
 668:  * Besides the pin-point glint, a torch lays a broad soft glow on the water
 669:  * under it - the smeared reflection of the flame itself. A wider lobe at a
 670:  * fraction of the gain.
 671:  */
 672: const TORCH_GLOW = 0.35;
 673: const TORCH_GLOW_GLOSS = 5;
