 726:  *
 727:  * Tested on the mirrored ray against the sun direction - a lobe in the sky,
 728:  * not on the surface - so it moves across the pool and shivers with the
 729:  * rings. The exponent is what a hazy sun looks like: wide enough to be a
 730:  * patch, tight enough to have an edge.
