 892:  * Has to sit under the *finest* octave in the field, not the coarsest. At
 893:  * SNOW_COVER's scales the third octave lands at 0.3 * 2.13 * 2.31 = 1.48
 894:  * repeats per tile, a period of 0.68 tiles, so 0.2 gives a little over three
 895:  * samples per period - it under-reads the finest octave's slope slightly and
 896:  * invents nothing.
 897:  *
 898:  * It tracks the drift scale: this was 0.08 while the drifts were a tile
