 908:  * channel floor drops - deeper than any drift, because it goes through them.
 909:  * `TRAIL_LIP` is the heap of shouldered snow raised along the rim: it rides
 910:  * on the map's soft edge (peaks where the map is half deep), so it is a
 911:  * bank on the slope and not a wall on a cliff. `TRAIL_CHURN` is the broken,
 912:  * turned-over snow on the floor. `TRAIL_STEP` is the gradient step for all
 913:  * three - a fifth of the drift step, because a rim is a tenth of a tile.
 914:  */
