  43: 
  44: /**
  45:  * The grass layer: blades standing on the tiles the splat map already draws
  46:  * as grass.
  47:  *
  48:  * The original had this pass and the clone never ported it -
  49:  * `TERRAIN_MAP_GRASS` is a constant nothing reads. `RenderTerrainFace` drew
  50:  * one vertical alpha-tested card per grass tile from `TileGrass01/02/03`
  51:  * (ZzzLodTerrain.cpp:1620-1675). This is that layer with the card replaced by
  52:  * geometry: real blades are opaque, so the whole layer costs no transparency,
  53:  * no sorting and no alpha test, and a cutout pass over the ground is by far
  54:  * the more expensive of the two.
  55:  *
  56:  * Lit entirely through `terrainLighting.ts` - the same bake, torches,
  57:  * cascades and roof mask the tile under each blade takes. A blade that is a
  58:  * shade off the ground it grows from is more obviously wrong than either
  59:  * would be alone, so there is no second opinion about the light here.
  60:  */
  61: 
  62: /** Tiles per block edge. 256 blocks over the map. */
  63: const BLOCK_TILES = 16;
  64: const BLOCKS_PER_SIDE = TERRAIN_SIZE / BLOCK_TILES;
  65: 
  66: /**
