 843:     // The blade being eaten, from the tip down.
 844:     //
 845:     // A dissolve and not a shrink. The blade's geometry stays whole and the
 846:     // fragment stage takes it away, so what the eye follows is an *edge*
 847:     // travelling down each leaf with a line of ember on it. Scaling the height
 848:     // instead - which is what this did first - is invisible: a field of blades
 849:     // getting shorter is a field getting slightly sparser, and at any distance
 850:     // that reads as nothing happening at all.
 851:     //
 852:     // The wobble is per blade, off the hash, so a patch does not burn as one
 853:     // straight line across.
 854:     if (vBurn > 0.0) {
 855:       float wobble = ${DISSOLVE_WOBBLE.toFixed(3)}
 856:         * sin(vV * ${DISSOLVE_FREQ.toFixed(1)} + vSeed * 40.0);
