 870: 
 871:       // And the blade alight, which is the fire itself.
 872:       //
 873:       // This was a sprite: the skills' flame recipe, thrown at points around
 874:       // the rim. A sprite is a picture of a fire standing near some grass, and
 875:       // however small it is made it is still a billboard hanging over the
 876:       // field rather than a blade that is burning. The blade already knows
 877:       // where its own cut is and how hot the ground under it is, so the flame
 878:       // is drawn on the leaf, in the band just below where the leaf is being
 879:       // eaten.
 880:       //
 881:       // Three sines out of phase, on the blade's own hash, so each one
 882:       // flickers to its own clock and a burning patch is never in step. The
 883:       // band breathes with the flicker rather than only brightening, because a
 884:       // flame that changes only in intensity reads as a lamp.
